From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:28:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 065/342] app_server: blend_line32() writes an opaque alpha

The fast path of FillRect() in B_OP_ALPHA with B_ALPHA_OVERLAY blended
the colour channels into a temporary line and copied it back with the
alpha byte left as whatever was on the stack. meson_hdmi keys its video
overlay by the frame buffer's alpha, so while a video played, the icon
stripe of every notification showed garbage stripes through it. The
other B_ALPHA_OVERLAY paths write 255, and so does this one now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/app/drawing/drawing_support.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/servers/app/drawing/drawing_support.h b/src/servers/app/drawing/drawing_support.h
index e387bf65d6..5895ba102d 100644
--- a/src/servers/app/drawing/drawing_support.h
+++ b/src/servers/app/drawing/drawing_support.h
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@ blend_line32(uint8* buffer, int32 pixels, uint8 r, uint8 g, uint8 b, uint8 a)
 		t[0] = ((p.data8[0] * a) >> 8) + b;
 		t[1] = ((p.data8[1] * a) >> 8) + g;
 		t[2] = ((p.data8[2] * a) >> 8) + r;
+		t[3] = 255;
+			// opaque, as the other B_ALPHA_OVERLAY paths leave it; the
+			// stack's garbage showed a video overlay through (meson_hdmi
+			// keys it by the frame buffer's alpha)
 
 		t += 4;
 		s += 4;
